## Stack

- **n8n** — orchestration
- **Alpaca API** — live market data + paper trade execution
- **Google Gemini** — AI decision engine (structured JSON output) + report writer
- **Google Sheets** — trade log and daily summary storage
- **Gmail** — automated daily report delivery

## Key challenges solved

- **Preventing over-trading**: a cooldown filter blocks repeated signals within a 5-minute window, so the AI can't fire the same trade multiple times off noisy data.
- **Filtering weak signals**: a 5-condition guardrail rejects low-confidence decisions and invalid price/quantity values before they ever reach order execution.
- **Structured AI output**: uses a structured output parser to force the AI's response into a strict JSON schema (action, confidence, qty, entry, SL, TP) instead of parsing free text.
- **Price correction on BUY orders**: a dedicated validator step corrects entry prices before order placement to avoid slippage-related rejections.

## Setup

This workflow expects the following, none of which are included in the export:

| Requirement | Used for |
|---|---|
| Alpaca paper trading API key + secret | Market data + order execution |
| Google Gemini API credential | AI decision engine + report writer |
| Gmail OAuth2 credential | Sending daily report emails |
| Google Sheets OAuth2 credential | Trade log + daily summary sheets |

Replace the Google Sheets document ID with your own before running. Workflow must be set to **Active** to run on schedule. Currently configured for AAPL only — additional symbols can be added by duplicating the trigger → fetch → format chain into the same AI agent.

## Note

This is a portfolio export of a working trading agent, currently running against Alpaca's **paper trading** environment (simulated, no real funds). It requires active Alpaca, Gemini, Gmail, and Google Sheets credentials to run.
